hello and welcome to med simplified  while coronavirus cases continue to soar  across the world  we have another reason to worry the  emergence of bird flu  after many states in india reported  death of birds mostly non-domesticated  bird flu or avian influenza was  confirmed in kerala  rajasthan madhya pradesh haryana  and himachal pradesh high alert has also  been sounded in maharashtra  several states which have been reporting  deaths of birds including crows and  migratory species  are scrambling to have samples tested  for the virus  similar incidents were reported in  countries like japan  china south korea netherlands uk  belgium denmark france and many more  countries  the sudden drop in demand in prices is  compounding the losses of millions of  small poultry farmers  in an industry that only recently  started to recover  from the covet outbreak that hugely  impacted sales during 2020.  avian influenza also called avian flu or  bird flu  is an illness that usually only affects  birds  there are many different strains of bird  flu virus but the most commonly seen  and most deadly form of the virus is  called influenza  a or the h5n1 virus  the last time avian influenza hit india  in 2006  it seriously disrupted the functioning  of poultry industry  the government intervened first  confirming the presence of the bird flu  and then destroying numerous birds to  control the spread of the virus  so in this video we will talk about what  is bird flu  the virus that causes bird flu we will  discuss  whether this disease can spread from  human to human and whether you should  stop  eating poultry right now or not  bird flu also known as avian influenza  or avian flu  is a variety of influenza caused mostly  by the group a  influenza viruses so influenza viruses  are a type of  rna viruses and they can be divided into  four main groups  influenza a influenza b influenza c  and influenza type d viruses influenza  a-type viruses usually infect wild  aquatic birds  and often spread to poultry birds  causing bird flu  and can spread to humans also we will  discuss more about the type a viruses  later  influenza b viruses almost exclusively  infect humans  whereas influenza c viruses infect  humans  dogs pigs sometimes causing  both severe illness and local epidemics  now let's  look at how these viruses damage living  organisms  now influenza virus can only replicate  inside a living cell  first the virus binds to the surface of  the cell and injects  its genetic material which in this case  is a viruses rna  inside the living cell then the genetic  material of the virus  takes over the molecular machinery of  our living cells  and instructs ourselves to make more  copies of the viruses genetic material  slowly the cell gets filled with the  viral rna and dies  the viral rna then assembles a membrane  over it  and in the last it exits the host cell  the current epidemic of avian influenza  is caused by the h5 and  8 strain of the influenza a virus before  this  mostly the h5n1 strain of the virus has  led to most epidemics among the birds  while h5n8 presents only a low risk to  humans  it is highly lethal to wild birds and  poultry  in india several states have reported  positive tests for avian influenza  among poultry and many types of  non-domesticated birds also  among these states kerala is the most  affected  as per the kerala government over 69 000  birds including ducks and chickens were  curled and eggs have also been destroyed  in some districts to contain the spread  of h5n8 strain of the bird flu  the northern state of himachal pradesh  reported the death of more than 3000  birds  from the disease mostly bar-headed geese  at a wildlife sanctuary  in india the disease spread mostly  through migratory birds  entering the country during the winter  season  the avian influenza virus can jump from  species to species and  infect humans from an infected bird the  first case of infection in humans was  reported in hong kong  in 1997 when a poultry farm worker  caught the infection from infected birds  human infections have been reported only  among people  who are poultry handlers and people who  deal with the sale of live animals  the high mortality rate in humans almost  60 percent  is the main cause of concern about the  spread of bird flow  so it is very important that you take  all possible precautions while the  outbreak lasts  people with co-morbidities or aged above  65 are the most vulnerable  pregnant women infants aged below 2 are  also vulnerable to the infection  the common symptoms of bird flow in  humans are  runny nose sneezing or sore throat in  the initial stages  while in the later stages the virus can  cause fever  fatigue body pain chills dry cough  and headaches now let's look at some of  the precautions you should take  regarding this avoid consuming uncooked  or partially cooked eggs and chicken  cooking meat at high heat  can kill the virus avoid coming in  direct or close contact with infected  poultry  the virus can enter your body if you  touch your eyes  nose or mouth after touching the  infected bird  you can also get the virus if you touch  a surface contaminated with a bird's  excretions  such as their stools or saliva the virus  can also be transmitted from large  infected droplets in the air  when in close contact with the infected  bird  now let's answer the most important  question regarding bird flu  and that is should you stop eating  poultry and eggs right now  scientifically there is little evidence  to support the fact that bird flu can  spread to healthy people  via eggs and meat after thorough washing  and cooking  it is safe to eat them and they do not  act as a carrier of the virus  who has said the same whenever any meat  or poultry is exposed to heat  it kills any germs pathogens or viruses  which may be present on the surface or  even beneath it  hence cooking thoroughly makes it safer  for use  while cooking an egg make sure that the  yellow yolk becomes firm  and avoid eating runny eggs during the  course of this  outbreak this is also a precautionary  step  people should take before consuming any  type of non-veg food  according to experts a cooking  temperature of up to 70 degrees celsius  that reaches all the parts of eggs or  meat is good to kill germs  also make sure to buy the poultry from  organic trusted places  slaughtered meat or handling of dead or  diseased  birds before cooking should be strictly  avoided during this epidemic  lastly also remember that we are already  in the middle of a widespread pandemic  wash your hands with good quality soap  and water for 20-30 seconds before  and after cooking as long as you follow  good hand hygiene  take care of your source of poultry and  cook it well  there is really no reason to worry  so guys thank you so much for watching  this video  i hope you liked the video if you did  support us by hitting the like button  below  and you can also support math simplified  by clicking the join button below  or joining us on patreon page all links  are in the description box below  thank you so much for watching see you  in the next video
 

